  "published": "2026-08-27T17:10:46.193Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0 — MailKit under the hood, plus a first-class async API. No breaking changes: IMail and every existing public member keep their signatures.\n\nADDED:\n- IMailAsync.SendMailAsync(...) with CancellationToken support. Mail now implements both IMail and IMailAsync.\n- New constructor Mail(VSmtpMailConfig) for configuration coming from environment variables or the Options pattern; throws ArgumentNullException on null.\n- Multi-targeting: netstandard2.0, netstandard2.1, net8.0, net9.0, net10.0 (was net6.0 only).\n\nIMPROVED:\n- Transport moved from System.Net.Mail.SmtpClient to MailKit 4.17.0. Port 465 (implicit SSL) now works — the old client only supported STARTTLS and always failed on 465. Connection security is negotiated automatically for 465 / 587 / 25.\n- Missing SMTP settings now raise InvalidOperationException instead of a NullReferenceException when the configuration binds to nothing.\n- Attachments with an empty or unparsable content type fall back to application/octet-stream instead of failing the send.\n\nTECHNICAL:\n- Deterministic builds, SourceLink, embedded untracked sources and a .snupkg symbol package.\n- .NET analyzers at the latest analysis level with code style enforced in build; the library builds warning-free across all five target frameworks.\n- Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions / .Binder upgraded to 8.0.x.\n- xUnit test project covering the public contract: settings validation, message assembly, recipient/CC mapping, HTML vs plain body, attachment skipping and content types.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/ozakboy/ozakboy.Mail/blob/main/docs/en/changelog.md\nMigration guide (1.0.x → 1.1.0): https://github.com/ozakboy/ozakboy.Mail/blob/main/docs/en/migration.md",
